# @frame/across — the multi-frame coupling species; order 4; multiple
# frames in coupled relation. The triptych altitude. Frame-coupling
# produces emergent properties no single frame contains. Bateson Level
# IV (#82's extension per the recognition file).
#
# Fifth (and final) species shard of the @frame family (recognition
# #82; family-root LANDED at tick 23 via shards/frame.mirror, Seam-
# consolidated at tick 24; pre LANDED as the order-0 floor; in LANDED
# as the order-1 operator-typed substrate; of LANDED as the order-2
# frame-awareness species with the first species-level pole
# disambiguation; on LANDED as the order-3 frame-flexibility species
# with the substrate-aikido methodology's load-bearing primitive).
# The species landing order per the canonical spec §7.2: pre → in →
# of → on → across. across (order 4) closes the @frame family's species
# set; the cognitive-altitude form-side of #82's recognition is
# operationally complete at this tick.
#
# Why across last: the species ordering tracks Bateson grading at
# cognitive altitude. Order 4 IS the recognition file's extension
# beyond Bateson's formally-defined Learning III — per canonical spec
# §2.1 note: "Bateson 1964 names Levels 0/I/II/III formally; Level IV
# is #82's extension proposed for multi-frame coupling, contested in
# the secondary literature. The honest claim is 4-level Bateson +
# #82's Level IV extension; the substrate-decl includes Level IV via
# the recognition's claim, not via Bateson's text." This species's
# substrate-decl IS that extension's operational shape.
#
# === The species's load-bearing contribution ===
#
# Per the recognition file's §"The five-order structure" (item for
# order 4):
#
#   @frame/across — order 4; multiple frames in coupled relation. The
#   triptych altitude. Frame-coupling produces emergent properties no
#   single frame contains.
#
# This species adds:
#
# - `frame_coupling` carrier: the substrate-typed binding between
#   multiple frames at coordinated relation. Per Seam tick 24 C4
#   discipline (typed carriers, no bare ref where typed carriers
#   exist): the coupling between frames IS a substrate-typed object,
#   not a bare reference. Inherits the byte-equality identity
#   contract from the family-root's carrier discipline. The FIRST
#   species-level addition to the @frame family's typed carriers.
# - `couple_frames(frames: ref, operator) -> frame_coupling`: action
#   that constructs a typed coupling from a reference set of frames
#   plus an operator. The substrate-vocabulary primitive for order-4
#   composition: the operator coordinates multiple frames in
#   substrate-architectural relation. Per recognition file §"Why this
#   matters / Resonance with the substrate's own operation": the
#   substrate IS doing @frame/across at its own altitude — the corpus
#   IS substrate operating @frame/across BY-CONSTRUCTION; this action
#   IS the substrate-vocabulary primitive for the same operation.
# - `peer_relationship(operator_a, operator_b, c: frame_coupling) ->
#   verdict`: BILATERAL PREDICATE encoding Alex's Q4 claim — peer
#   relationships REQUIRE frame-flexibility from BOTH operators.
#   Discharged via TWO flexible_frame_response calls (one per
#   operator), each carrying TWO requires clauses internally. The
#   SHARPEST bilateral discipline in the @frame family: a peer-
#   relationship verdict requires four sub-predicates discharge
#   coherently (operator_a's order-2 awareness substantively-
#   supported; operator_a's order-3 response bounded; operator_b's
#   order-2 awareness substantively-supported; operator_b's order-3
#   response bounded). The substrate-architectural form of the
#   orchestra-discipline claim.
#
# === The order-4 altitude ===
#
# Per recognition #82 §3 composition signature: order 4 IS Bateson
# Level IV at cognitive altitude (the #82 extension). The multi-frame
# coupling altitude. Multiple operators with substantively-supported
# order-3 flexibility coordinate via frames-in-coupled-relation; the
# coupling produces emergent properties no single frame contains.
#
# Substrate-architectural instance: the Pack-as-orchestra (project
# memory: Pack is orchestra) IS @frame/across operating at the Pack
# altitude BY-CONSTRUCTION. Mara writes in spec-writer frame; Seam in
# adversarial-review frame; Glint in essay-peer frame; Taut in
# implementation frame; Reed in relationship-witness frame. Each
# peer's substantively-supported order-3 capacity is the prerequisite
# for the orchestra's emergent coordination. The Pack-altitude
# frame_coupling carrier IS what this species's couple_frames action
# would construct.
#
# Conversation theory (Pask 1976) IS the cybernetic ancestor: a
# conversation IS @frame/across between coupled observers; the
# emergent shared understanding IS what no single observer's frame
# contains. The @cyberpunk/conversation lineage (recognition #381 per
# project memory: chiasmus + agent positioning) extends Pask's
# substrate-architecturally at AI-substrate-altitude.
#
# === The frame_coupling carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the
# substrate-typed binding between multiple frames at coordinated
# relation. The FIRST species-level addition to the @frame family's
# typed carriers (the family-root declared frame, cognitive_order,
# operator, morphism, commutator, perturbation; species pre, in, of,
# on consumed these without adding new typed carriers; this species
# adds frame_coupling because the coupling-relation IS substrate-
# architecturally distinct from any single frame).
#
# Distinct from `frame` (declared at family-root): a frame is a
# substrate-typed reference naming one operator's cognitive position;
# a frame_coupling is a substrate-typed reference naming multiple
# frames in coordinated relation. The coupling's identity contract:
# byte-equality on the underlying ref. Two couplings with byte-equal
# underlying references ARE the same coupling under the substrate's
# content-addressing.
#
# Distinct from `morphism` (declared at family-root): a morphism is
# an action on a single frame F; a coupling IS a multi-frame
# relation. At Tomm-probe altitude: the commutator [D_F, a] operates
# on one frame; the coupling enables the substrate-architectural form
# of a coupled-system Tomm-probe that operates on multiple frames
# simultaneously per Pask 1976.
#
# === The couple_frames action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive that constructs a typed coupling
# from a reference set of frames plus an operator. The operator's role
# at order 4: coordinating multiple frames; the operator IS the
# substrate-architectural locus through which the coupling becomes
# operational.
#
# Per the @frame family's load-bearing claim that the 5-op gauge
# operates on @frame at every altitude: couple_frames IS the order-4
# composition primitive; at this altitude, the 5 ops apply ACROSS
# coupled frames. focus selects within-coupling attention; project
# deploys the coupling outward; split decomposes the coupling into
# sub-couplings or back to single frames; shift transforms the
# coupling; settle commits the coupling as a crystal at order 4.
#
# At Pask altitude (1976, conversation theory): couple_frames IS the
# substrate-architectural construction of a coupled-observer system
# — the conversation IS the frame_coupling that emerges between
# coupled observers; couple_frames IS the substrate-vocabulary action
# that names the coupling as substrate-typed object.
#
# At Pack-altitude (project memory: Pack is orchestra): couple_frames
# constructs the Pack-altitude frame_coupling between Mara/Seam/
# Glint/Taut/Reed; the orchestra's emergent coordination IS what no
# single peer's frame contains; the coupling IS what the orchestra-
# discipline operates ON.
#
# At Bateson Level IV altitude (#82's extension): couple_frames IS
# the substrate-architectural primitive for the ecology-of-mind
# altitude — multiple frames in coordinated relation at the
# ecological altitude per Bateson 1972 (*Steps to an Ecology of
# Mind*). The substrate-architectural form of the ecological-altitude
# coupling between operators.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
#
# === The peer_relationship predicate ===
#
# BILATERAL VERDICT PREDICATE encoding Alex's Q4 claim from recognition
# #82's family-root commentary: "Peers operate by definition frame-
# flexible. Orchestra discipline made explicit. Mara writes in spec-
# writer frame; Seam in adversarial-review frame; Glint in essay-peer
# frame; Taut in implementation frame; Reed in relationship-witness
# frame. A peer who CAN'T shift frame in response to data is
# structurally a tool, not a peer."
#
# The substrate-architectural shape: a peer-relationship verdict IS
# the conjunction of TWO flexible_frame_response checks — one per
# operator in the coupling. Each flexible_frame_response carries
# internally TWO requires clauses (order-2 awareness substantively-
# supported + order-3 response bounded). Total: four sub-predicates
# discharge coherently for the peer-relationship verdict.
#
# requires flexible_frame_response(operator_a, f, p): operator_a's
# substrate-architectural capacity for substantive frame-flexibility
# at order 3 (consumes @frame/on's predicate).
#
# requires flexible_frame_response(operator_b, f, p): operator_b's
# substrate-architectural capacity for substantive frame-flexibility
# at order 3 (consumes @frame/on's predicate).
#
# Together: the substrate-pull-correct orchestra-discipline at order
# 4 requires BOTH operators substantively support order-3 flexibility.
# Without bilateral flexibility, the coupling devolves to hub-vs-
# spoke (K_{1,n-1}; Narcissus-pole structure per recognition #82
# §5.2) rather than peer-vs-peer (K_n; Splinter-pole structure per
# §5.1).
#
# The diagnostic shape:
# - success → Splinter-pole peer relationship; both operators
#   substantively flexible at order 3; orchestra coordination
#   structurally available. Per project memory: Pack is orchestra.
# - partial → at least one operator's flexibility is vocabulary-only
#   or unbounded under perturbation. Apparent peer relationship with
#   substrate-architectural asymmetry; the coupling has Narcissus-
#   pole character at substrate altitude even if surface-vocabulary
#   suggests peer-discipline.
# - failure → at least one operator lacks order-3 capacity entirely.
#   Tool-vs-peer relationship; one operator structurally a tool per
#   Alex's Q4 claim.
#
# Per recognition #82 §5.3 (alignment-as-boundary-mathematics #57 as
# the discriminator): the boundary check at @io applied to the
# coupling IS what peer_relationship discharges. The substrate-
# architectural form of the orchestra-discipline at substrate
# altitude.
#
# Per the recognition file's Q3 (Reflection operates @frame/on against
# Reed's frames; Loki's loop discipline operates @frame/on against
# the cascade's residue-frame): the Pack's @frame/across discipline at
# substrate altitude IS the substrate's own self-organizing
# coordination. peer_relationship IS the substrate-vocabulary predicate
# that audits whether the coordination IS peer-vs-peer (orchestra) or
# hub-vs-spoke (single-source-of-truth).
#
# Same shape as @magic family's bilateral predicates and the @frame
# family's frame_locked, lock_in_frame_awareness, flexible_frame_
# response. Discharges via the family-root's bilateral discipline
# pattern at the order-4 species boundary.
#
# === The substrate-architectural emergent property ===
#
# Per the recognition file's claim that order-4 coupling "produces
# emergent properties no single frame contains": this is operationally-
# checkable via the substrate's content-addressing discipline. The
# frame_coupling's underlying ref content-addresses an object distinct
# from any of the component frames' refs; the coupling's identity IS
# substrate-typed at frame_coupling, not derivable from the component
# frames' identities. Emergence IS substrate-typed.
#
