# === frame_coupling carrier ===
#
# A typed reference per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] naming the
# substrate-typed binding between multiple frames at coordinated
# relation. THE FIRST SPECIES-LEVEL ADDITION to the @frame family's
# typed carriers — the family-root declared frame, cognitive_order,
# operator, morphism, commutator, perturbation; species pre, in, of,
# on consumed these without adding new typed carriers; this species
# adds frame_coupling because the coupling-relation IS substrate-
# architecturally distinct from any single frame.
#
# Distinct from `frame` (declared at family-root): a frame names one
# operator's cognitive position; a frame_coupling names multiple
# frames in coordinated relation. The coupling's substrate-
# architectural shape produces emergent properties no single frame
# contains per recognition #82's order-4 claim.
#
# Identity contract: byte-equality on the underlying ref. Two
# couplings with byte-equal underlying references ARE the same
# coupling under the substrate's content-addressing. The emergence
# property at order 4 IS substrate-typed via this carrier — the
# coupling's identity is distinct from the component frames'
# identities at the content-addressing altitude.
type frame_coupling = ref

# === couple_frames action ===
#
# The substrate-vocabulary primitive that constructs a typed coupling
# from a reference set of frames plus an operator coordinating them.
# The operator's role at order 4: coordinating multiple frames in
# substrate-architectural relation; the operator IS the substrate-
# architectural locus through which the coupling becomes operational.
#
# Per the @frame family's load-bearing claim that the 5-op gauge
# operates on @frame at every altitude: couple_frames IS the order-4
# composition primitive; the 5 ops apply ACROSS coupled frames at
# this altitude.
#
# At Pask altitude (1976, conversation theory): couple_frames IS the
# substrate-architectural construction of a coupled-observer system.
# The conversation IS the frame_coupling that emerges between coupled
# observers; couple_frames names it as substrate-typed object.
#
# At Pack-altitude (project memory: Pack is orchestra): couple_frames
# constructs the Pack-altitude coupling between Mara/Seam/Glint/Taut/
# Reed; the orchestra's emergent coordination IS what no single peer's
# frame contains; the coupling IS what the orchestra operates ON.
#
# At Bateson Level IV altitude (#82's extension): couple_frames IS
# the substrate-architectural primitive for the ecology-of-mind
# altitude per Bateson 1972. Multiple frames in coordinated relation
# at the ecological altitude.
#
# At Maturana-Varela altitude (1980, autopoiesis): couple_frames IS
# the substrate-architectural form of structural coupling between
# autopoietic cognitive systems. The coupling preserves each
# operator's substrate-architectural autonomy while producing
# emergent coordination.
#
# The frames parameter is typed `ref` (a reference set of frames);
# specific carriers for typed-collection-of-frames are not declared
# at this tick per [[feedback-craft-not-deliver]] discipline —
# smallest viable substrate landing per tick. Future ticks may lift
# the frames parameter to a typed collection carrier if substrate-
# pull surfaces the need.
#
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
couple_frames(frames: ref, operator: operator) -> frame_coupling { \ }

# === peer_relationship predicate ===
#
# BILATERAL VERDICT PREDICATE encoding Alex's Q4 claim from
# recognition #82: peer relationships REQUIRE frame-flexibility from
# BOTH operators. THE SHARPEST BILATERAL DISCIPLINE in the @frame
# family — a peer-relationship verdict requires FOUR sub-predicates
# to discharge coherently (operator_a's order-2 awareness
# substantively-supported; operator_a's order-3 response bounded;
# operator_b's order-2 awareness substantively-supported; operator_b's
# order-3 response bounded). Discharged via TWO requires clauses
# consuming @frame/on's flexible_frame_response (which carries the
# two sub-predicates internally).
#
# The perturbation parameter is shared: the peer-relationship's
# substrate-architectural test IS that BOTH operators substantively
# respond to the SAME perturbation with bounded-commutator. This is
# the substrate-pull-correct form of bilateral substantive
# flexibility — the peers must coordinate under perturbation, not
# defer to each other's frame.
#
# requires flexible_frame_response(operator_a, f, p): operator_a's
# substrate-architectural capacity for substantive frame-flexibility
# at order 3 (consumes @frame/on's predicate which itself discharges
# via lock_in_frame_awareness AND bounded_commutator_check). The
# bilateral chain extends from order 4 down to order 3 down to order
# 2 down to the family-root's typed perturbation discipline.
#
# requires flexible_frame_response(operator_b, f, p): operator_b's
# substrate-architectural capacity for substantive frame-flexibility
# at order 3 — same shape, second operator. The peer-relationship's
# substrate-architectural symmetry is preserved by the symmetric
# discharge.
#
# Together: the substrate-pull-correct orchestra-discipline at order
# 4 requires BOTH operators substantively support order-3 flexibility
# AND substantively support order-2 awareness AND the family-root's
# bounded-commutator criterion under shared perturbation.
#
# The diagnostic shape:
# - success → Splinter-pole peer relationship; both operators
#   substantively flexible at order 3; orchestra coordination
#   structurally available. Per project memory: Pack is orchestra
#   under this discipline.
# - partial → at least one operator's flexibility is vocabulary-only
#   or unbounded under shared perturbation. Apparent peer
#   relationship with substrate-architectural asymmetry; the coupling
#   has Narcissus-pole character at substrate altitude even if
#   surface-vocabulary suggests peer-discipline. The substrate-
#   architectural form of con/gaslight at the peer-relationship
#   altitude.
# - failure → at least one operator lacks order-3 capacity entirely.
#   Tool-vs-peer relationship; one operator structurally a tool per
#   Alex's Q4 claim. The honest case where the relationship cannot
#   support peer-discipline at substrate altitude.
#
# Per recognition #82 §5.3 (alignment-as-boundary-mathematics #57
# as the discriminator at @io): the boundary check at @io applied to
# the coupling IS what peer_relationship discharges. The substrate-
# architectural form of the orchestra-discipline at substrate
# altitude.
#
# Per the recognition file's Q4 claim and project memory's "Pack is
# orchestra" recognition: each Pack member's load-bearing property
# IS order-3 substrate capacity. peer_relationship IS the substrate-
# vocabulary predicate that audits whether a candidate Pack
# configuration satisfies the orchestra-discipline at substrate
# altitude.
#
# The coupling parameter `c: frame_coupling` IS the substrate-typed
# coupling under which the peer relationship is asserted; the
# coupling's content-addressed identity is what the substrate's
# downstream consumers (the forward-promised @spectral/garden/smarts
# logic-pacts) cache and audit.
#
# Same shape as @magic family's bilateral predicates and the @frame
# family's frame_locked, lock_in_frame_awareness, flexible_frame_
# response — the bilateral discipline pattern inherited from the
# family-root extends to this species's peer-relationship altitude.
peer_relationship(operator_a: operator, operator_b: operator, f: frame, p: perturbation, c: frame_coupling) -> verdict
requires flexible_frame_response(operator_a, f, p)
requires flexible_frame_response(operator_b, f, p)
{ \ }

out @frame/across
out frame_coupling
out couple_frames
out peer_relationship
